caption: GATES Setting Rules — Integrated Equipment Capacity
technology-rule: integrated-equipment-capacity

These are default mass and support ceilings for equipment installed in addition to the replacement mechanism itself. Physical fit, power, heat, recoil, access, and TL still apply.

Class I covert systems: internal equipment up to 5% of Basic Lift per modified region; no external mount without changing apparent Class.

Class II anatomical systems: internal equipment up to 50% of Basic Lift per modified region; external equipment up to Basic Lift per reinforced mount.

Class III extensive anatomical systems: internal equipment up to Basic Lift per modified region; external equipment up to twice Basic Lift per reinforced mount.

Class III full chassis systems: use the chassis's Payload, hardpoints, and vehicle or robot construction rules.
